XThis is official patch #1 for othello v1.3; please apply it.
X
XIt makes the following changes.
X
X       * From Valerie Haecky <vmh@Eng.Sun.COM>
X         The default setting for remarks is now set to no. The remark
X         output when remarks is turned off has been changed to
X         "Okay, no more remarks from me".
X
X       * From Valerie Haecky <vmh@Eng.Sun.COM> and
X              Mike Stump <cbcscmrs@gaia.csun.edu>
X         The starting position is the wrong way round. d4 and e5 are
X         white, d5 e4 black, and black starts the game.
X
X       * From Valerie Haecky <vmh@Eng.Sun.COM> and
X              Mike Stump <cbcscmrs@gaia.csun.edu>
X         The numbering of the board is wrong: letters across, numbers down.
X
X       * From Daniel Yang <dyang@doorknob.Sun.COM>
X         Two minor changes needed for spelling and syntax errors in the
X         manual page.
X
X       * From Mike Stump <cbcscmrs@gaia.csun.edu>
X         The README file has the domain mail address as richb@Aus,Sun.COM.
X         This should be richb@Aus.Sun.COM
X
X       * From Eric R. Jorgensen <jorgy@boulder.colorado.edu>
X         The images.h file has a spurious ';' character at the end of
X         one of the #include lines.
X 
X       * From Mike Stump <cbcscmrs@gaia.csun.edu> and
X              John Rosauer <johnr@extro.ucc.su.oz> and
X              Linton Miller <lmiller@comp.vuw.ac.nz>
X         Othello doesn't display correctly with the X11 and XView versions
X         on a monochrome screen.
X
X       * From Mike Stump <cbcscmrs@gaia.csun.edu>
X         Some machines do not have the usleep library function. A new
X         definition has been added to the Makefile. This should be
X         uncommented if your machine doesn't have usleep.
X
X       * From Steve Misrack <steve@ucsd.edu>
X         Othello doesn't work in when run under SunView started in inverse
X         mode. An extra command line option (-i) has been added, and the
X         SunView driver adjusted accordingly.
X
X       * From Hugues.Leroy%irisa.fr@munnari.oz
X         Some old machines with old compilers don't accept struct parameters.
X         Various functions have been adjusted to handle this.
X
X
